    "title": "Motorcyclist identified in fatal crash with semi-truck in Centreville - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anna Chen ,\n9 hours ago\nCENTREVILLE, Va. ( DC News Now ) — The motorcyclist who died in a crash with a semi-truck has been identified.\nOfficers with the Fairfax County Police Department (FCPD) responded to a two-vehicle crash in the 12800 block of Route 29 on May 19, just before 2 p.m.\nPREVIOUS COVERAGE: 1 dead after motorcycle, tractor-trailer crash in Braddock There, officers found a 2005 Ducati motorcycle and a 2016 Mack Semi Truck were involved in a crash.\nThe motorcyclist, identified as 22-year-old Mikhail Perry of Fairfax, died at the scene.\nPreliminarily, FCPD said Perry was headed northbound on Route 29, and the truck was headed southbound.\nThe truck was trying to make a U-turn when Perry hit it.\nAs of now, FCPD said it believes that speed was a factor in the crash.\nAnyone with information is asked to call 703-280-0543.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to DC News Now | DC, Virginia, Maryland News, Weather, Traffic, Sports Live.\n2",
